  "description": "Add-on for IntentSharp: guardrails as versioned rule files. Keep what your application's model calls, agent tools and data operations may do (allow and deny lists, patterns, ranges, counts, JSON Schema checks, and limits such as time limits and result caps) in YAML or JSON rule files in a document store, listed in one manifest, instead of in compiled code. Every check runs in your process with no model call: an operation proceeds only when an enforced rule covers what it touches, a deny always wins, and a rule file that fails to load keeps its last good version in force. Every decision names the rule set, its document and its version. A rule written as intent text can be compiled into deterministic checks, and no model decides when a check runs. An AI edit to a rule file is validated and then takes effect by default; an edit that widens access is flagged so that your own code can hold it for review. Add this package to IntentSharp when rule sets live in files; a project that supplies its own rule sets in code through IGuardrailSource needs only IntentSharp, without this package's YAML and JSON Schema dependencies. Our estimate for IntentSharp in a typical business application is 20 to 40% less application code. Commercial software, not open source: evaluate free for 30 days on development and test systems; after that, business use needs a paid license, and production use needs one from the first day (intentsharp.com/pricing).",
